#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114992 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "51a437bf-2a11-5eba-a046-4770d41214ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4720" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, gives the result of the product $EA$." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=5R_{1} + R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation\n\n$$\nR_2:=5R_1+ R_2\n$$\n\nto $A$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114993 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4721" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$. Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation\n\n$$\nR_1:=R_1 - R_2\n$$\n\nto $A$.\n\nTo find $E$, we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid:=R_{1} - R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114994 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "0f08f8aa-63e3-500a-987e-e9888b9b0479" :question/math-academy-id "e-4722" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$:\n$R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad R_2:=R_2+3R_1$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid ↔R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{1}$\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + 3R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{2}$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A$, we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A$, we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A$:\n\n$$\nMissing \\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e52ce19-81ac-5c22-9902-7c2065196186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113896} {:answer/id #uuid "c9aa26a7-227e-5ab3-bc86-3a931f2ed899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113897} {:answer/id #uuid "d6102675-4954-502a-92cb-e4e546a7b8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113898} {:answer/id #uuid "dc54996a-49a9-503f-b175-35709d230755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113899} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e0442c-4b50-5d22-b23e-f0fa898968d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9aa26a7-227e-5ab3-bc86-3a931f2ed899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113897} :answer-field/id #uuid "0869fcde-eb4b-57de-a801-96cd55fafab0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113895}] :question/id #uuid "fd3b5a32-f5f9-54aa-b2af-a91ccc349130" :question/math-academy-id "q-42767" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix $A$:\n\n$R_{2}:=-2R_{2}, R_{1}↔R_{2}, R_{2}:=R_{2} + 3R_{1}$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication."}]}
